# infra/aws-poc — accepted misconfiguration residuals (cmw-sec-deploy-scan-gate, 2026-08-12)
#
# Used by deploy/security-gate.sh's `trivy config --severity CRITICAL` step. Every entry below is
# a deliberate, justified accept — not a blanket suppression. Re-evaluate whenever this security
# group changes.

# AWS-0104 — "security group rule should not allow unrestricted egress to any IP address."
# aws_security_group.app's egress block (security.tf) is a deliberate all-outbound-any-destination
# rule: the instance needs unrestricted outbound to pull from ECR, reach SSM, install OS packages,
# and let the SSM agent phone home — none of those destinations are fixed/listable CIDRs. Ingress
# is the side that's actually locked down (see security.tf's description: CloudFront's
# origin-facing prefix list only, no public SSH — SSM Session Manager instead). Open egress from a
# single-purpose instance is the conventional accepted risk here, same posture as most managed
# compute; tightening it to specific destination CIDRs would need to track AWS's own
# service-endpoint IP ranges by hand and re-verify on every AWS-side change, for marginal benefit
# on a POC-scale instance with no direct inbound path.
AVD-AWS-0104
